<p>Iranian officials and state media say a girls’ school in Minab, southern Iran, was struck during Saturday’s wider U.S.-Israeli attacks on Iran, causing heavy casualties. Reported death tolls have varied across Iranian statements and international coverage, ranging from “dozens” to 100-plus and as high as 148. The reports come as the U.S.-Israel military operation against Iran escalates. Iranian leaders condemned the incident while also trying to project continuity at the top of the state: Iran’s president called the attack “barbaric,” and officials said Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei was alive amid speculation about leadership casualties. U.S. and Israeli authorities have not publicly confirmed striking the school. That leaves key details—what was targeted, and why—unclear and disputed.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/bSQlOUACInkE-kNr139ROki7Zp2csZSZZsVWBhIFX44WeX6GvND5iuBQEca6PrdkrlsCB7cPkYa1yPqb7w24kWz_S_uCzeGLlor5E46FoqBcjGPOYlSd8786Ru85XgYAMMjOlMvFRkyMOhv9DggOh-VvIgePJokXxMKT_Die5xwZXBctqxwGkH02RfD6HWaITQKZzO7KtL9jD4f7Z_I-q0toXCeY0Pi3vesDed5LOW4EFfJQ2nNgMxs' alt='Rescue workers and residents search through the rubble after the bombing of a girls&#x27; elementary school in Minab, Iran, February 28, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Conflicting tolls: Iranian outlets and officials gave different casualty figures, highlighting the uncertainty as information trickled out from the site.</li><li>Two school sites: Reporting that reviewed the broader pattern of Saturday’s strikes described the Minab incident as one of two attacks that appear to have hit schools.</li><li>What was hit: Coverage described the site as a girls’ primary/elementary education facility in Minab, struck amid the wider U.S.-Israel operation.</li><li>Footage and rubble: Iranian state media aired images of extensive damage at the school as residents and rescue workers searched through debris.</li><li>Leadership opacity: Coverage also pointed to limited transparency about possible losses among senior Iranian figures, even as officials said Khamenei was alive.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Iranian government: President Masoud Pezeshkian condemned what he called a “barbaric” attack on a school after the U.S.-Israeli strikes. (<a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/irans-president-pezeshkian-condemns-barbaric-school-attack-following-us-israel-strikes-13984819.html'>Firstpost</a>)</li><li>Iranian state media: State media said a girls’ school in Minab was hit and framed the incident as a major civilian-casualty event. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/01/iran-s-state-media-say-100-killed-in-strike-on-girls-school-but-losses-among-the-regime-s-leaders-still-lack-transparency_6750971_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>US and Israel (as reported): The U.S. and Israel have not publicly confirmed that their strikes hit the school, as reporting noted claims about nearby elite military troops. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c1l7rvqq51eo'>BBC News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/055d7ee1-0002-4d86-931f-18f4687d4f8b'>Strike on Iranian primary school kills 148, authorities say</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/28/world/middleeast/iran-school-strike-us-israel.html'>Iran Says Dozens Are Killed in Strike on School</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/01/iran-s-state-media-say-100-killed-in-strike-on-girls-school-but-losses-among-the-regime-s-leaders-still-lack-transparency_6750971_4.html'>Iran&#x27;s state media say 100 killed in strike on girls&#x27; school</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-condemns-barbaric-attack-on-school-after-us-israeli-strikes-says-khamenei-is-alive/article70689136.ece'>Iran condemns &#x27;barbaric&#x27; attack on school after U.S., Israeli strikes; says Khamenei is ‘alive’</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href=